  "body": "## T-2380 \u2014 the log jail's keeper house, continuous palisade front and low gate\n\nA **partial** increment on the original picture-match ticket. **The match is not\nclaimed and T-2380 stays open**: both reference views were re-rendered against\nthis geometry and both record verdict `differs`, with the remaining differences\nwritten down.\n\n### What ships\n\n- **`log_jail_keeper_house`** \u2014 John Beach's house, the one Gale 1902 p51 puts\n  partly inside the jail enclosure facing Randolph. Built on a new **opt-in**\n  `keeper_gale_1902` layout of the native `frame_dwelling` archetype: the\n  pictured W/W/D front stations, two east-gable ground sash, a small loft light\n  and the stack at the pictured gable end.\n- **The compound** \u2014 the palisade now runs continuously across the front, and a\n  low framed, braced, hung gate (`log_jail_keeper_link`) stands on the house\n  side.\n- **The core is untouched.** `log_jail` keeps its mesh and its 12\u00b0 roof; only its\n  explicitly reconstructed access setback moves 1.30 m south, inside the ~20 m\n  site uncertainty its own record declares.\n\n### Provenance\n\nEverything numeric here is reconstruction and says so. One new liberty,\n`L-log-jail-keeper-compound-2380`, covers the footprint, position, documented\nrange, picture layout, construction, stories, wall height, roof pitch, plan,\npaint, glazing, shutters, porch and the simplified cladding; `L148` picks up the\ndealt siding stock and `L263`'s population count moves 691 \u2192 692. The house is\n`inferred`, never `documented`: Trowbridge's plate and Gale's recollection are\ntier-5, the plate is captioned **1836**, and the evidence ladder forbids a\ndocumented value resting on tier 5 alone. Andreas draws a different elevation\nand that disagreement is recorded rather than reconciled. Nothing backdates the\nfall-1835 court-house into the 1 July scene, and the roof is entered in the\nphysical-roof reconciliation as `inventory_eligible: false` \u2014 it stands in the\nscene and not in the 1835 count.\n\n### Native outputs \u2014 built here, on the pinned Blender\n\nNot carried in from anywhere. Built on this runner on Ubuntu 26.04 with the\nsha256-verified pinned **Blender 4.5.3** from `generators/blender.pin`:\n\n- master `assets/gltf/log_jail_keeper_house__frame_1835.glb` \u2014 70,712 bytes,\n  sha256 `431dc44f37bdcb2c7f705a5b17b65fe6a1cf748d077c337b699094c9b41752a8`\n- web derivative \u2014 20,632 bytes, sha256\n  `15eb2fbad5e1b8f464c30f7135297047896b4eff95f9168de6084e75e86f710e`\n  (pinned gltf-transform, via `tools/web_derivatives.sh`)\n\n**The frame family was qualified, not assumed.** The opt-in parameter refreshes\nthe input signature of all **271** existing `frame_dwelling` assets. All 271\nwere rebuilt on the pinned Blender and **every one came back byte-identical** \u2014\nthe opt-in moves no vertex of any other building. Their manifest rows carry only\na new `inputs_sha256`; no asset was removed, and no foreign registry row\n(including the K01 rows) was touched. An intermediate build of this very record,\nbefore the siding deal, reproduced the earlier packet's retained master and web\npair byte-for-byte (`03aafaa4\u2026` / `b1997083\u2026`), which is how the pinned\ntoolchain was checked before anything was committed.\n\n### The picture comparison \u2014 `differs`, with the differences named\n\nRe-rendered with `tools/photo_match.mjs` for both views, as a group (core +\nkeeper) with both enclosures. Side-by-sides are in the diff at\n`docs/RESEARCH/photo-match/log_jail/`. Two differences the increment **closes**\n(the keeper house was absent; the compound front and gate were absent); still\nopen, in both views:\n\n- the jail core reads **concealed behind the palisade**, where both pictures show\n  its log walls and roof standing clear \u2014 the palisade is too high for the core\n  against these pictures, or the core too low, and this increment settles\n  neither;\n- the compound's **relative proportions** are wrong against the plate;\n- the palisade is one flat mass where both pictures draw separate boards;\n- neither camera is solved \u2014 both carry `diagnostic_only: true`, so no framing\n  disagreement is promoted into a metric error.\n\nNo new photo follow-up ticket is filed (T-3153). T-2380 is released back to the\nqueue, open, with these differences on it.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `tools/validate.py` \u2014 **PASS**, 0 errors (schema, provenance, liberties\n  coverage, date gates, staleness: 0 stale assets).\n- `./tools/check.sh --part k/4` \u2014 run in the foreground, one call each; see the\n  checklist in the comments below for which parts were green at push time.\n- Sidecars recompiled, `tools/rederive.mjs --check` at its fixed point, resident\n  layer converged, and `tools/publish.sh` run before every gate.\n- The hosted dev gate and smoke on this PR are the merge gate.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
